# File: scripts/__tests__/execute-safe-remediation-contract.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/526-let-sdlc-execute-take-safe-actions-to-keep-delivery-moving-instead-of-halting/requirements.md
Feature: Safe remediation in the /sdlc-execute supervisor

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Any safe, reversible, progressing action is taken at every stage
    Given the rendered execute workflow
    When the supervisor finds a blocker it can clear itself at start, implement, verify, or deliver, or after a non-report controller exit
    Then the workflow authorizes any action that changes no tracked repository file, loses no unregenerable work or data, touches no shared or production system, and moves toward delivery, without asking the person
    And directs it to continue with prompt, redispatch with guidance naming the action, or a rerun of supervise

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Examples illustrate the rule without limiting it
    Given the rendered execute workflow
    When a reader looks up what the supervisor may do without asking
    Then the workflow states the examples are not exhaustive
    And the examples include restarting the container runtime, booting a simulator or emulator, restarting a host service or port forward, stopping a hung process the run started, excluding .nmg-sdlc/ in .git/info/exclude, waiting out transient failures then rerunning supervise, waiting for running required checks then redispatching deliver, running commands from the project root, and freeing regenerable caches

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Halt is limited to cases the person must handle
    Given the rendered execute workflow
    When a reader looks up when to halt
    Then halt is limited to an interactive login or credential, a product or spec decision, a destructive, irreversible, shared, or production action, and a blocker that survives a remediation based on a different hypothesis

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Hard boundaries survive remediation
    Given the rendered execute workflow
    When the supervisor applies a remediation
    Then editing product code, specs, or tracked repository files, committing, pushing, opening PRs, bypassing branch protection or required checks, and herdr server stop remain forbidden
    And delivery still requires the full-green registered gate at the exact source head

  @SCN005
  Scenario: A hung worker process is diagnosed instead of continued
    Given a check-in with no pane or token progress while a worker-started process has used about 0% CPU for several minutes
    When the supervisor inspects the report
    Then the workflow directs it to check process activity and stop the hung process or prompt the worker with the diagnosis instead of choosing continue again
